node_modules
.next
next-env.d.ts
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
.vercel

# Secrets. `.env.example` is the committed template; every real `.env*` is not.
# This was missing before auth landed, which is exactly the window in which the
# database password gets pasted into a file and committed.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
!.env.example

# Cesium's runtime assets, ~14MB, copied out of node_modules by
# tools/copy-cesium-assets.mjs on predev and prebuild. A build artifact, not
# source: committing it would put a vendored copy of the library in history and
# make it go stale the moment the cesium version moves. Vercel runs prebuild, so
# the deploy generates it the same way a local build does.
public/cesium

# Third-party checkouts dropped into this directory by hand. None of them are
# part of this project; they are reference material read locally. They were
# ignored by the previous root .gitignore, which went when the project it
# belonged to was removed, and without this they show up as untracked noise
# next to a clean tree.
#
# Ignored rather than deleted: they are someone's working copies, and a
# .gitignore entry costs nothing to undo.
#
# `lal-quest` is deliberately NOT listed. It is a separate app on its own
# branch (feat/lal-quest), and hiding it here would make it look absent.
/AdventureLog/
/TREK/
/Tourism-Recommendation/
/Tourism-Recommendation-System/
/ai-travel-planner/
/ai-travelassistant/
/makemydrivefun/
/trip-planner/
/research/
/.twin/
